SUMMARY:Mt. Mitchell to Winter Star\, 8.4mi\, 2\,900ft\, Fitness Hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Description:** Out and back diff
 icult\, rugged and challenging high mountain forrest hike with beautiful m
 ountain flora (picture)\, fauna\, and gorgous vistas. Trailhead begins on 
 the Black Mountain Crest Trail ( at Mt. Mitchel) from the picnic area (low
 er parking lot) to Winter Star Mountain. We will be hiking up and over pea
 ks that are above 6\,000' (Mt. Mitchel's elevation is over 6\,400 feet).. 
 This hike includes some rugged rocky sections with rope assist and ladder 
 climbs. This hikes is specifically for conditioned hikers. Please be sure 
 of your hiking ability before signing on.\n\n**PACE:** All fitness hikes h
 ave a brisk steady pace\, adjusting for trail conditions\, and regrouping 
 as needed. Due to steepness of grade and rugged conditions we will probabl
 y average about 2.5 mph.\nIf you sign up and change your mind even if on a
  waitlist\, change your RSVP to "not attending" to free up your reservatio
 n.\n\n**Weather:** Cancelations due to wet or predicted stormy weather con
 ditions will be announced on or before 7:00 am hike day. Temperatures are 
 usually 10+ degrees colder than Asheville and often windy.\n\n**CAR POOL:*
 * Two options I will be at the Ingles Market on Weaver Blvd\, Weaverville 
 by the Gas pumps leaving at 8:25 am\, or Asheville hikers can meet at the 
 Folk Arts Center parking lot on the BRP at 8:25 am.. Please post where you
  plan to meet otherwise see you at the Mt. Mitchel picnic area trailhead a
 t 9:30.\n\nDriving to Mt. Mitchell picnic area: From Asheville\, take the 
 Blue Ridge Parkway north/east past the various Craggies to Route 128. Turn
  left toward Mt. Mitchell. Drive all the way to the Mt. Mitchell parking l
 ot. The picnic area is to your left just as you enter the parking lot on t
 he lower level.\n\nDogs are welcome\, but have a leash handy in case we ru
 n into other hikers or dogs.\n\nHIKE LEVELS This one is **level 9-10.**\n\
 nHike Level (1) Up to 600 feet of elevation gain. Level (2) 600'- 900'\; L
 evel (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4) 1200' - 1500'\; Level (5) 1\,500' - 1\,8
 00'\; Level (6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'\; Level (7) 2\,100' - 2\,400'\; Level (8
 ) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level **(9) 2700' - 3000'** Level (10) 3000' - 4000'\;
  ULTIMATE HIKES are hikes > 4\,000' elevation gain\; We post 3-4 of these 
 hike challenges a year.\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe organizer of thi
 s trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the or
 ganizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in th
 is event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume a
 ll risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result 
 of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that yo
 u agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314983022
 /
